<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela cabinet approve aluminum sale contracts.</title>
<headline>Venezuela cabinet approve aluminum sale contracts.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuela's economic cabinet approved Wednesday proposed sales contracts for the country's aluminum sector which will be formally presented for Congressional discussion on Thursday, Information Minister Fernando Egana said.</p>
<p>Investors view the privatization of the four aluminum firms Alcasa, Venalum, Carbonorca and Bauxilum as a test of the government's mettle to push through structural reforms, and the sales contracts are expected to encounter stiff resistance in Congress.</p>
<p>Thirteen companies have qualified to bid for the aluminum companies, including Alcoa, Gencor, Alumax, Reynolds Metals Co, Norsk Hydro ASA and RTZ Corp.</p>
<p>((-- Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
